WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.868
-Emma Thompson, welcome back.
You are awesome.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:06.100
You are the most fun.
You look gorgeous.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.601
Welcome, welcome, welcome.
-Thank you so much.

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:11.634
-Thank you for being here.
-Oh, I'm so happy to be back.

00:00:11.634 --> 00:00:13.200
I can't believe
it's been so long.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.501
-It has been a while.
-I'm completely exhausted.

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:17.133
-From doing that?
-Yeah, just from doing that.

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:19.767
It's literally pathetic.

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:22.334
-I like having you here during
this time of year

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:24.334
because you're on
every television.

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:27.334
"Love Actually" is playing
on every channel, every hour,

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:28.367
and it's so good.

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:29.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:31.567
And it's my favorite scene,
which I've always told you,

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:34.567
but your scene, the
heartbreaking, saddest scene.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:35.767
You're so
awesome and phenomenal.

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:37.734
I'm like, "How do you do that?"
That was just --

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:38.868
-Do you want me to do it
for you now?

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:41.667
-No, no, no, please don't.
No, no, no.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:43.167
Do you ever watch it?
-I don't think it would work.

00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:44.234
-Do you ever see it?
Do you ever --

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:45.834
-No.
-No, you don't watch that. No.

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:47.100
-It was 20 years ago.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.534
-I know, but it's kind of fun
to put it on.

00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:52.200
You go, "Oh, I remember where we
were when we were doing that."

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.200
-Not really.
-No?

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.968
-No, you just say,
"Was I being --

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:57.601
I don't think
I was very well-paid for that.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:01:00.634
And that was that
terrible trailer with the loo

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:03.000
that really stank
and had that sort of --

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.834
These are just
the things you remember.

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:07.534
-How many fans have sent you
Joni Mitchell CDs?

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.234
-I have a separate house
for those.

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:11.467
-Just built with all CDs.

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:12.634
Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:14.033
-Oh, you know what I really want
to ask you about,

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:16.868
is your husband
was on the U.K. version of

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:18.000
"Dancing with the Stars."

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.467
"Strictly..."

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:20.901
-"Strictly Come Dancing."

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:22.033
-Yes.
-Yes.

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:23.701
-And he was great.
-I made him do it.

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:26.934
I said, "It's going to be
so much fun."

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:29.167
So not fun.

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:30.367
-It's not, huh?

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:33.601
-No, because the training
is just unbelievable.

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:36.801
I mean, he was so tired.

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:38.367
He lost all this weight.

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:41.334
I was like, "Oh, God,
is he going to survive?"

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:45.868
You know, and then,
the worst of it is,

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:47.767
okay, so, you go and do it,

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:49.601
and everyone loves you
and you're just the best,

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:52.334
but you absolutely
have to keep saying

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:53.968
that you're living
your best life.

00:01:53.968 --> 00:01:55.701
If you're not
living your best life

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:56.767
and it's better than anything,

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:58.501
including the
birth of your children

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:00.434
and, you know, anything,

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:02.868
then you're kind of
not really living up to it.

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:06.200
And then,
when you get thrown off,

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:09.234
it's sort of like
being pushed off a moving bus.

00:02:09.234 --> 00:02:12.300
So if you know how to roll,
it's okay,

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.601
but if you don't,
like we didn't --

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:14.834
You know, and I'm like,

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.634
"But I'm here wearing
a sparkly pink jacket.

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:17.834
This can't happen."

00:02:17.834 --> 00:02:21.067
And then he just --
He, like, face-planted.

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:23.033
And I'm like,
"Okay, get up, get up, get up.

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:25.467
Don't show fear.
Don't show fear."

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:27.167
Because this is
the moment where they come,

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:28.734
and the dogs tear you.

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:31.868
They tear you.
And we went --

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:33.167
-The critics come out.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:34.400
-Yes.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.000
-And then we went back
and got the whiskey out

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.234
and we went around the corner

00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:38.501
and bought
a packet of cigarettes.

00:02:38.501 --> 00:02:41.501
And we were, like, smoking
six -- Like, "We're fine.

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:43.334
No, it's fine."
-In high school. Oh, my God.

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:44.934
-[ Coughs ]

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:47.200
It was really traumatic.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.033
-I was thinking that you were
going to get up on there

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:50.267
and start dancing with him.

00:02:50.267 --> 00:02:52.200
Did you -- Were you --
-It didn't occur to me.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.033
No, I would not have done that.

00:02:54.033 --> 00:02:55.767
Because it would have been
really embarrassing.

00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:57.868
-No, it's not --
But your dancing is fantastic.

00:02:57.868 --> 00:02:58.934
-Well, that's very kind.

00:02:58.934 --> 00:03:00.901
But it would have been
inappropriate.

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:02.834
-No, it would have been so cool.

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:06.767
You dancing at the Adele concert
was fantastic, by the way.

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:08.701
I don't know if
any of y'all saw this,

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:10.701
but when Emma Thompson
was at the Adele concert

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:12.834
and you were dancing,
they got you on videotape.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:14.701
Let's just show
a little clip of this.

00:03:14.701 --> 00:03:16.968
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:32.767
-I see you dancing.
You've been dancing all night.

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:34.067
Hi.

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:36.367
-I like that one where you...

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:38.534
-Yeah.
"Get up, get up," I'm going.

00:03:38.534 --> 00:03:41.133
-It's like Mick Jagger.
-Oh, my God.

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:43.300
-It was -- I loved that.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:46.033
-Because all the celebrities
were sitting downstairs,

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:47.033
and they were all being --
sort of just sitting there,

00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:48.033
being good.

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:49.934
I'm like, "Get up!

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:51.367
We've been in COVID
for two years.

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:52.501
We're out."

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:54.434
It's the first time
we had all been out.

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:58.167
-Party! Exactly right.
-Oh, thank God, we can get out.

00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:00.701
-That was fantastic,
and everyone loved it.

00:04:00.701 --> 00:04:03.067
And they're going to get to
see you in a musical.

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:04.634
-Yeah.
-Yeah, "Matilda."

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:05.801
Roald Dahl.
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:05.801 --> 00:04:07.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:10.367
Do it perfect.
-Thank you.

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:11.634
Let's talk about this.

00:04:11.634 --> 00:04:13.400
Because you kind of got
your start -- right? --

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:14.467
kind of in musicals.

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:15.467
Didn't you do a musical
on the West End?

00:04:15.467 --> 00:04:17.200
-I did. I did it for 15 months.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:20.734
It was a
tremendously cheerful musical,

00:04:20.734 --> 00:04:23.834
so after nine months,
I was clinically depressed,

00:04:23.834 --> 00:04:25.067
because, you know, it was...

00:04:25.067 --> 00:04:27.300
♪ Doin' the Lambeth walk ♪
♪ Oy! ♪

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.267
♪ Anytime you're Lambeth way ♪

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:31.501
It was that, sort of the
Cockney number, you know?

00:04:31.501 --> 00:04:34.601
And it was ever so cheerful.
So, yes, I was deeply depressed.

00:04:34.601 --> 00:04:36.234
-Yeah, you go, "I can't do this.
I can't be that happy."

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:37.300
-No, you can't.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.834
Seriously,
it's not good for you.

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:42.934
Forced cheeriness for 15 months,
eight shows a week.

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:44.801
-Will destroy you.
-It would kill anyone.

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:46.634
-It would kill anyone, yeah.

00:04:46.634 --> 00:04:49.100
But this was the perfect amount,
"Matilda."

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.501
-Yeah.
-And you got all the kids.

00:04:50.501 --> 00:04:51.534
-Yeah.
-But look at you.

00:04:51.534 --> 00:04:53.734
This is you as Miss Trunchbull.

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:55.868
It doesn't even look like you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:55.868 --> 00:04:57.267
Look at you.

00:04:57.267 --> 00:05:00.234
Can you make that face?
How do you even make that face?

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:02.234
-Mm. Mean.

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:03.667
And were the kids supposed to be
afraid of you?

00:05:03.667 --> 00:05:04.868
-They were.

00:05:04.868 --> 00:05:06.167
Yeah, they were supposed to be
afraid of me,

00:05:06.167 --> 00:05:07.901
but, of course,
I just walked on set,

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:10.934
Oh, "Nanny McPhee,
Nanny McPhee!"

00:05:10.934 --> 00:05:13.400
I'm like, "No, not Nanny McPhee!
Shut up!

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:16.167
I am Trunchbull now! Shush!
Be afraid!"

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:17.701
And they were all going...
[ Laughs ]

00:05:17.701 --> 00:05:19.400
"Oh, you're funny."

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:20.634
And the director's going,

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:22.701
"Will you please stop
hugging the children?"

00:05:22.701 --> 00:05:25.801
Because I loved them so --
They were so fantastic,

00:05:25.801 --> 00:05:27.200
these kids, honestly.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:30.367
-Yeah, it's going --
They released some dance thing

00:05:30.367 --> 00:05:31.667
on TikTok I saw,
like, a behind the scenes.

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:32.667
-Oh, my God. Yeah.

00:05:32.667 --> 00:05:34.667
-And it is already viral
on TikTok.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.901
Every kid is doing this.
They're so talented.

00:05:36.901 --> 00:05:38.367
-They're just extraordinary.

00:05:38.367 --> 00:05:40.567
And they had worked for months

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:41.834
and months and months
beforehand.

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:43.334
They're so extraordinary.
-I want to show everybody.

00:05:43.334 --> 00:05:46.133
Here's a clip.
Here's "Matilda," everybody.

00:05:46.133 --> 00:05:48.400
-♪ Have you ever
smelled anything worse

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:52.200
than that smell of rebellion? ♪

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.567
♪ The stench of revolt ♪

00:05:55.667 --> 00:06:01.667
♪ The reek of insubordination ♪

00:06:01.667 --> 00:06:05.033
♪ A whiff of resistance ♪

00:06:05.033 --> 00:06:08.501
♪ The pong of dissent ♪

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:13.400
♪ And I will not stop
till you are squashed ♪

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:16.734
♪ Till this rebellion
is quashed ♪

00:06:16.734 --> 00:06:21.968
♪ Till glorious,
sweaty discipline has washed ♪

00:06:21.968 --> 00:06:25.701
♪ This sickening stench

00:06:25.701 --> 00:06:34.734
awa-a-a-a-y ♪

00:06:34.734 --> 00:06:37.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:37.067 --> 00:06:39.234
-What are you talking about?!

00:06:39.234 --> 00:06:41.734
-Oh. Stop it.

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:45.234
-I have never given a clip --
a standing ovation of a clip.

00:06:45.234 --> 00:06:47.534
That was amazing!

00:06:47.534 --> 00:06:50.067
You can sing.
That was unbelievable.

00:06:50.067 --> 00:06:52.167
And that was live singing?
-Yeah.

00:06:52.167 --> 00:06:55.334
And, actually, that last note,
my legs were shaking

00:06:55.334 --> 00:06:59.300
because I was on top of that
80-foot structure with,

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.901
you know, really nothing but
a small wire

00:07:01.901 --> 00:07:03.200
holding me to the thing.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:05.033
And I thought,
"Oh, please, please don't."

00:07:05.033 --> 00:07:07.067
And then I just -- But there
was nothing you could do.

00:07:07.067 --> 00:07:08.200
-Just hit that note and get out.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:10.100
-You just hit the note
and go for it.

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.400
-♪ Ahhhh ♪
-Yeah, "Ahhhh."

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:13.300
-Oh, it's so good.

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.400
I also want to talk about,
quickly, if you can,

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:16.534
"Good Luck to You, Leo Grande."

00:07:16.534 --> 00:07:17.634
-Yes.

00:07:17.634 --> 00:07:19.534
-You were phenomenal
in this, as well.

00:07:19.534 --> 00:07:21.234
And this is a different movie,
by the way.

00:07:21.234 --> 00:07:22.767
-Very different.
-Very different.

00:07:22.767 --> 00:07:25.367
This is not for the children.
-No. No.

00:07:25.367 --> 00:07:27.167
-Not for the kids, this one.
-No.

00:07:27.167 --> 00:07:29.968
-But, man, you're on every list,
award buzz

00:07:29.968 --> 00:07:32.000
because you just knocked it
out of the park, as always.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.300
But do you want to set up
what that movie

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.567
is about so people know?

00:07:34.567 --> 00:07:36.801
-It's about an
ex-religious-education teacher

00:07:36.801 --> 00:07:40.067
who's widowed and has been
widowed for two years

00:07:40.067 --> 00:07:44.367
and who decides to hire
a very much younger

00:07:44.367 --> 00:07:48.901
28-year-old sex worker because
she's never had an orgasm.

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:50.167
-Mm.
-Mm-hmm.

00:07:50.167 --> 00:07:52.267
-Yep. So totally different movie
than "Matilda."

00:07:52.267 --> 00:07:54.200
[ Laughter ]

00:07:54.200 --> 00:08:00.300
-But you do feel that Trunchbull
could do with a sex worker.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:02.501
Or possibly be one.
She might be one.

00:08:02.501 --> 00:08:05.567
She might be somebody's
idea of absolute bliss.

00:08:05.567 --> 00:08:09.501
I can see some very interested
faces over there.

00:08:09.501 --> 00:08:12.267
-We love having you on the show.
Please come back more often.

00:08:12.267 --> 00:08:13.734
We love you.
Emma Thompson, everybody.

00:08:13.734 --> 00:08:16.100
Roald Dahl's
"Matilda the Musical,"

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:18.000
is in select theaters
this Friday

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.000
and on Netflix December 25th.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.400
We'll be right back
with Guillermo del Toro.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.300
Stick around.
♪♪

